# Copy to .env.local (gitignored — see .gitignore's `*.local`).
#
# There is deliberately no admin key here any more. Through M7 this file
# carried VITE_ADMIN_API_KEY, and Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed variable
# into the built JavaScript — so the key that gates enrolling machines into
# the fleet shipped inside the bundle, readable from devtools by anyone who
# loaded the page. M8 (ADR-012) replaced it with real user accounts: you sign
# in, and the browser holds only a short-lived token scoped to your account.
#
# Create your account on the orchestrator host:
#   python -m scripts.create_user --username <you> --role ADMIN
#
# Nothing secret belongs in this file. Anything put here ends up in the built
# bundle and is public to everyone who loads the dashboard.

# The orchestrator's real, network-reachable base URL — used only to build
# the one-line enroll command shown in the "Add a node" modal (a peer agent
# dials this directly; it is NOT proxied through the dashboard's dev server).
# Defaults to http://localhost:8090 (this repo's compose stack) if unset.
VITE_ORCHESTRATOR_URL=http://localhost:8090
